+// The same question asked of a live tab: its last committed URL and its last
+// committed entry's redirect chain. A tab with no contents, or nothing
+// committed yet (the entry's own first load is still in flight), is not at
+// home -- there is nothing to write back from it anyway.
+bool IsTabAtPinnedUrl(const tabs::TabInterface* tab, const GURL& pinned_url);
+
+// helium-fork M3.10-r2: whether a bound row wears the "/" drift mark and
+// offers "Back to Pinned URL". Deliberately *not* !IsAtPinnedUrl(): a tab
+// whose first navigation has not committed yet has no URL to compare, and
+// what it is loading is the pinned URL itself, so reading it as drifted
+// flashes a "/" beside the favicon every time the user opens a pinned page
+// (user 2026-08-24: 「第一次打开网页的时候，加载的就是最开始 pin 过的 URL，
+// 不应该出现这个符号」). |has_committed_navigation| is false until the tab's
+// first main-frame navigation commits.
+//
+// The write-back gate keeps asking IsAtPinnedUrl instead: "we do not know
+// where this tab is yet" must block writing the entry's title and favicon,
+// but must not accuse the row of having drifted.
+inline bool IsDriftedFromPinnedUrl(bool has_committed_navigation,
+                                   const GURL& tab_url,
+                                   const GURL& pinned_url,
+                                   base::span<const GURL> redirect_chain) {
+  return has_committed_navigation &&
+         !IsAtPinnedUrl(tab_url, pinned_url, redirect_chain);
+}
+
+// The same question asked of a live tab.
+bool IsTabDriftedFromPinnedUrl(const tabs::TabInterface* tab,
+                               const GURL& pinned_url);
